6. DEFENSIVE HANDLING DUTIES

For every permitted use, you must:

(a) use the least intrusive method reasonably available;
(b) minimize collection and immediately stop if use may cause harm or exceed
    authorization;
(c) protect all credentials, personal information, confidential information,
    and scan results against unauthorized access;
(d) avoid placing live credentials or identifying target details in public
    issues, logs, demonstrations, datasets, or reports;
(e) securely delete data that is not necessary for the authorized purpose;
    and
(f) report verified exposure only through lawful, confidential channels to
    the affected owner or an appropriate authority.

